<code>assert \old(this.containsKey(key)) => !this.containsValue(\result);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.containsKey(key)) => !this.containsKey(key) && (\old(this.get(key)) == \result || (\old(this.get(key)) == null && \result == null));</code>

Explanation:
- `\old(this.containsKey(key))` checks if the key was present in the map before the removal.
- `!this.containsKey(key)` ensures that the key is no longer present in the map after the removal.
- `(\old(this.get(key)) == \result || (\old(this.get(key)) == null && \result == null))` ensures that the value returned by the `remove` operation is the value that was previously associated with the key. This handles the case where the value could be `null`.
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.containsKey(key)) => !this.containsKey(key) && \old(this.get(key)) != \result;</code>

This assert statement checks that if the key was previously in the map (`\old(this.containsKey(key))`), then after the `remove` operation, the key is no longer in the map (`!this.containsKey(key)`) and the value returned by the `remove` operation (`\result`) is not present in the map anymore (`\old(this.get(key)) != \result`).
